# Line endings.
#
# Compakt is developed on Windows and built on Linux, so the repository
# normalises to LF and lets each checkout decide. Two exceptions: .bat
# files are read by cmd.exe, which mishandles LF-only, and Inno Setup
# scripts are conventionally CRLF.
#
# Getting this wrong is not cosmetic. A shell script or Makefile checked
# out with CRLF fails on Linux with an unhelpful "bad interpreter" or
# "command not found", which is a bad hour to spend.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.iss text eol=crlf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.dll  binary
*.so   binary
*.pyd  binary
*.pakt binary
